lifeos-nix patch f-pulse-module-flags — make Pulse module enable/disable flags actually work

PROBLEM
  Two gaps made per-module enable flags dead: (1) loadPulseConfig() only populated ~13
  module keys in the returned config and NEVER merged PULSE.user.toml module sections, so
  config.X for any user-only or unmapped module (amber, assets, books, conduit, menubar,
  projects, usage, doctor, memory, tab-freshness, local_intelligence, hypotheses,
  derived_watch, siri) was undefined; (2) ten "surface" modules were imported with no
  enabled gate at all. Net: `config.X?.enabled !== false` always passed → modules loaded
  regardless of PULSE.toml/PULSE.user.toml. Observed 2026-08-11: local_intelligence loaded
  despite the N1/K10 OFF flag (no egress — its fetch is POST-only and never triggered —
  but the flag was simply inert). K10 user-tier toggles (amber/assets/books/conduit OFF)
  were entirely ignored.

FIX (1 file, pulse.ts)
  loadPulseConfig — parse PULSE.user.toml and merge its module sections over PULSE.toml
  (user wins, per-section shallow merge), then populate config.X for every module from the
  merged map (`mod(k)`). Existing keys switch parsed.X → merged.X so user overrides apply.
  loadModules — gate the ten always-loaded surface modules behind
  `if (config.X?.enabled !== false)` (default-on; false disables). PulseConfig type gains
  the previously-missing module keys. Jobs merge is unchanged (loadConfig).

